## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around data governance, cross-region containment, and traceability after a data-leak fault in a deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and evidence tagging
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle gates
- REST API design for CAPA management with linked logs/traces
- Regional leakage metrics and false positive handling
- RCA templates and canary rollback for data sinks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA data model in TypeScript
type CAPA = {
  capa_id: string;
  incident_time: string;
  data_class: string;
  evidence_refs: string[];
  lineage: string;
  owner: string;
  remediation: string;
  status: 'IDENTIFY'|'CONTAIN'|'INVESTIGATE'|'REMEDIATE'|'VERIFY'|'CLOSED';
  RCA_id?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate with an existing audit log system?
- How would you enforce access controls for CAPA modification?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests ability to design a production-grade CAPA for a multi-tenant data platform, emphasizing isolation, auditability, and scalable rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped CAPA data model with evidence and artifacts
- Immutable links to logs/traces and resource metadata
- Lifecycle state machine and canary-based enforcement
- Per-tenant metrics (recurrence, MTTR, spillover rate)

## Code Example
```javascript
// TypeScript interface for CAPA
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  policyId: string;
  incidentId: string;
  evidenceLinks: string[];
  artifacts: string[];
  affectedResources: string[];
  dataClassification: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle CAPA versioning and backward compatibility?
- How to simulate cross-tenant leakage in a canary without impacting production?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a complete CAPA flow for policy drift in a multi-tenant data catalog, tying data classification, access control, and observability into a repeatable remediation process.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model with tenants, assets, and evidence
- Region-aware lifecycle and RBAC integration
- Linked logs and lineage for traceability
- Canary rollout and RCA templating

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal CAPA data model (TypeScript-like)
type CAPA = {
  incidentId: string;
  tenants: string[];
  assets: string[];
  policyId: string;
  evidence: string[];
  rootCause: string;
  correctiveActions: string[];
  containmentTime: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce tiered access for CAPA data in a multi-tenant RBAC model?
- How would you gauge canary rollout success (metrics/thresholds) and trigger rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of drift in a multi-tenant streaming system with region isolation, ensuring containment without collateral impact. It also probes data lineage, governance, and rollout discipline.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with tenant scope, region, evidence, ownership, and lineage
- Region-tenant gated lifecycle to prevent cross-tenant bleed
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with linked logs/traces
- Tenant-scoped metrics: containment MTTR, drift score, recurrence rate, false positives
- RCA template and canary rollback plan for sessionization logic changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: CAPA data model (conceptual)
class CAPA {
  constructor(id, tenantId, region) {
    this.id = id;
    this.tenantId = tenantId;
    this.region = region;
    this.evidence = [];
    this.rootCause = null;
    this.actions = [];
    this.owner = null;
    this.state = 'DETECTED';
    this.timestamps = {};
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test isolation between tenants during a canary rollout?
- How would you handle cross-tenant drift if tenants share resources?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a data-path incident into a systematic CAPA plan, from data model to evidence mgmt and preventive action. Evaluates clarity, traceability, and practical canary-based rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model
- State machine
- Evidence management and RCA
- Region-aware metrics
- Canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Type definitions for CAPA (illustrative)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  evidence: string[];
  rootCause: string;
  correctiveAction: string;
  preventiveAction: string;
  status: 'proposed'|'in_progress'|'implemented'|'verified'|'closed';
  region: string;
  severity: 'low'|'medium'|'high';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you structure region-aware metrics and dashboards?
- What RCAs templates and safeguards would you require before closing a CAPA?
